---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="SwapLoader Hooklift Hoists | Equip Solutions Group"
  description="SwapLoader hooklift hoists from 12,000 to 50,000 lb capacity, plus the ST-1614 hooklift trailer, subframes and accessories. Independent rep support from spec to delivery.">

  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap page-hero-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Manufacturer line</p>
      <h1>SwapLoader Hooklift Hoists</h1>
      <p>One truck, unlimited bodies. Swap a dump body for a flatbed, a container, a water tank or a plow setup and put one chassis to work all year instead of parking three.</p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Get a hoist quote</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/parts/#swaploader">SwapLoader parts</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="split">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">The case for a hooklift</p>
          <h2 style="font-size:var(--step-3);text-transform:uppercase;">Buy bodies, not trucks</h2>
          <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1rem;">A second body costs a fraction of a second truck &mdash; and it does not need a driver, a plate, insurance or a parking spot. A hooklift turns one chassis into whatever the week demands, and the swap takes minutes from the cab.</p>
          <ul class="checks" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
            <li><strong>Hauling and dumping</strong> without dedicating a truck to either.</li>
            <li><strong>Drop and go.</strong> Leave the container on site and keep the chassis working.</li>
            <li><strong>Seasonal swing.</strong> Plow and spreader in winter, dump and flatbed the rest of the year.</li>
            <li><strong>Non-CDL options.</strong> The light-duty models open the Class 4&ndash;6 market without a CDL driver.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="ph ph--tall">Photo &mdash; hoist mid-swap, container coming off<br>Recommended 900&times;1200</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Model line</p>
        <h2>Capacities from light duty to 50,000 lb</h2>
        <p>Published manufacturer specifications. Body length and hook height determine what will actually fit your chassis and your existing bodies &mdash; call before you order so we get the CA dimension right.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table class="specs">
          <caption>SwapLoader hoist and trailer models</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col">Model</th>
              <th scope="col">Capacity</th>
              <th scope="col">Body length</th>
              <th scope="col">Hook height</th>
              <th scope="col">Typical fit</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">SL-110</th><td>12,000 lb</td><td>9&prime;&ndash;13&prime;</td><td>36&Prime; / 54&Prime;</td><td>Class 4&ndash;6 light duty, non-CDL</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">SL-112</th><td>12,000 lb</td><td>10&prime;&ndash;15&prime;</td><td>36&Prime; / 54&Prime;</td><td>Class 4&ndash;6 light duty, longer bodies</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">ST-1614</th><td>12,000 lb <span class="muted">(16,000 lb GVWR)</span></td><td>12&prime;&ndash;14&prime;</td><td>36&Prime; or 36&Prime;/54&Prime;</td><td>Trailer &mdash; hooklift capability without a truck build</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">SL-214</th><td>20,000 lb</td><td>12&prime;&ndash;18&prime;</td><td>36&Prime; or 36&Prime;/54&Prime;</td><td>Single-axle medium duty</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">SL-240</th><td>24,000 lb</td><td>12&prime;&ndash;18&prime;</td><td>54&Prime; or 54&Prime;/62&Prime;</td><td>Roll-off and container work</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">SL-2418</th><td>24,000 lb</td><td>10&prime;&ndash;13&prime;</td><td>54&Prime;</td><td>Shorter bodies, tight wheelbase</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">SL-520X</th><td>50,000 lb</td><td>17&prime;&ndash;24&prime;</td><td>62&Prime; or 62&Prime;/54&Prime;</td><td>Heavy tandem and tri-axle</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="small muted" style="margin-top:1rem;">Additional models fill in between these capacities. If your requirement sits between two rows, call &mdash; there is usually a model that lands closer than the chart suggests.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="plate-grid">
        <div class="plate">
          <div class="plate-code">Also available</div>
          <h3>Subframes &amp; Accessories</h3>
          <p>The hoist is half the order. Subframes, cab controls, tarp systems, lighting, container guides and hardware get spec'd at the same time so the upfit shop is not improvising.</p>
          <ul class="checks" style="margin-top:1rem;">
            <li>Subframes matched to chassis and body</li>
            <li>Patented adjustable jib on light-duty models</li>
            <li>Optional patented U-Locks</li>
            <li>Control and hydraulic options</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="plate">
          <div class="plate-code">Fleet &amp; public sector</div>
          <h3>Government Market</h3>
          <p>Municipal and county fleets are the clearest case for a hooklift: one chassis covering plow, spreader, dump, flatbed and container duty across the budget year instead of four vehicles depreciating in a yard.</p>
          <ul class="checks" style="margin-top:1rem;">
            <li>Spec support for bid and RFP language</li>
            <li>Multi-body configurations off one chassis</li>
            <li>Product registration and warranty paperwork handled</li>
            <li>Parts and manual access after delivery</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--dark on-dark">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Before you order</p>
        <h2>Five things that decide the model</h2>
        <p class="lede">Get these right on the phone and the build goes clean. Get them wrong and the hoist shows up correct on paper and useless in the yard.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="checks">
        <li><strong>Chassis CA and wheelbase.</strong> Determines which hoists physically mount and how the body sits.</li>
        <li><strong>Body length &mdash; existing and future.</strong> If you already own containers, the hoist has to match them, not the other way round.</li>
        <li><strong>Hook height.</strong> 36&Prime;, 54&Prime; or 62&Prime; changes what bodies you can pick up. Dual-height options exist for a reason.</li>
        <li><strong>Real loaded weight.</strong> Capacity ratings are for the loaded body, not the empty one. Scrap and aggregate get heavy fast.</li>
        <li><strong>Who is upfitting.</strong> Shop scheduling is often the longest item in the lead time. We plan around it up front.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Start a spec</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Send me your chassis and what you haul"
    body="I will come back with the model that fits, the options worth having, and a written number with lead time and freight in it.">
    <a class="btn" href="/contact/">Request a Quote</a>
    <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="tel:+15157200800">Call +1 515 720 0800</a>
  </CtaBand>

</BaseLayout>
